'''Season four''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on March 19, 2007, on the [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] network.

To avoid direct competition with [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]'s ''[[American Idol]]'', ''Dancing with the Stars'' changed time slots from [[Dancing with the Stars (US season 3)|the previous season]]. This season, the performance show aired on Mondays and the results show aired on Tuesdays. No elimination took place the first week in order to allow viewers two weeks to see all of the couples perform both Latin and ballroom dances. This season was broadcast on [[BBC One]] in the [[United Kingdom]] on Sunday afternoons.{{Citation needed|date=September 2022}}

On May 22, [[Olympic Games|Olympic]] short-track [[speed skater]] [[Apolo Anton Ohno]] and [[Julianne Hough]] were crowned the champions,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rizzo |first=Monica |author2=Michelle Tan |date=May 23, 2007 |title=Apolo Anton Ohno Wins Dancing with the Stars |url=http://www.people.com/people/article/0,,20039899,00.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090601191225/http://www.people.com/people/article/0,,20039899,00.html |archive-date=June 1, 2009 |access-date=August 11, 2009 |work=People}}</ref> while [[NSYNC]] singer [[Joey Fatone]] and [[Kym Johnson]] finished in second place, and boxer [[Laila Ali]] and [[Maksim Chmerkovskiy]] finished third.

==Cast==
===Couples===
This season featured eleven celebrity contestants. Actor [[Vincent Pastore]] was originally announced and partnered with [[Edyta Śliwińska]], but pulled out after one week of rehearsals. He was replaced by [[John Ratzenberger]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/DancingStars/story?id=2912176 |title=ABC News: John Ratzenberger Joins Cast of 'Dancing With the Stars' |publisher=Abcnews.go.com |date=2007-03-02 |access-date=2010-04-23 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090923211724/http://www.abcnews.go.com/Entertainment/DancingStars/story?id=2912176 |archive-date=2009-09-23 |url-status=live }}</ref> 
